{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.PagedSpectralSequence","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Quotient.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FiniteDimensional.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.eulerChar_bump_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.eulerChar_bump_eq","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/EulerCharacteristic.lean#L273-L299","doc":"**Euler characteristic is page-independent.**\n\nThe alternating sum of page ranks over a window is unchanged by turning the\npage — with **no collapse hypothesis**. The window hypothesis `hsupp` is\nabout where the differential is nonzero, not about it vanishing.\n\nThis is the other half of the asymmetry. An index of the shape\n`Δ_λ = (−1)^{n(λ)} dim V_λ` is a term of such a sum, so it can be evaluated\non whichever page is accessible; the individual `dim V_λ` cannot\n(`finrank_bump_eq_iff`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.sum_sgn_imRank_prev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.sum_sgn_imRank_prev","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/EulerCharacteristic.lean#L228-L271","doc":"**The cancellation.** Reindexed along `prev`, the incoming corrections are\nexactly minus the outgoing ones.\n\n`hsupp` is the finite-window hypothesis: every cell carrying a nonzero\ndifferential image lies in the window together with its target. Some such\nhypothesis is unavoidable — without it the sums are over infinitely many\ncells — and this is the weakest form that makes the reindexing legitimate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.eulerChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.eulerChar","kind":"def","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/EulerCharacteristic.lean#L224-L226","doc":"Signed rank sum over a finite window of cells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.finrank_bump_of_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.finrank_bump_of_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/EulerCharacteristic.lean#L214-L220","doc":"Consistency with `PagedSpectralSequence`: collapse gives an isomorphism, and\nan isomorphism gives equal ranks — the forward direction of\n`finrank_bump_eq_iff` reached the other way. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.finrank_bump_eq_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.finrank_bump_eq_iff","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/EulerCharacteristic.lean#L202-L212","doc":"**An individual page rank is page-independent exactly under vanishing.**\n\nHalf of the asymmetry this file exists to state: `dim E_r^c` survives\npage-turning only when both adjacent differentials die at `c`. That is a\ncollapse statement, and it is what the corpus does not have for the Gröbner\nfiltration — hence no `dim V_λ`. Contrast `eulerChar_bump_eq`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.finrank_bump_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.finrank_bump_add","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/EulerCharacteristic.lean#L175-L200","doc":"**The local rank identity.**\n\nTurning the page costs exactly the two differentials adjacent to the cell:\nthe one out of it (whose kernel it passes to) and the one into it (whose\nimage it quotients by).\n\nStated additively because `ℕ` subtraction is a trap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.finrank_incoming","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.finrank_incoming","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/EulerCharacteristic.lean#L159-L173","doc":"The incoming subobject has the rank of the incoming image: the `comap` along\n`(ker d_c).subtype` is an isomorphism onto it because `d ∘ d = 0` puts that\nimage inside the kernel, and `reindex` is an isomorphism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.imRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.imRank","kind":"def","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/EulerCharacteristic.lean#L154-L157","doc":"Rank of the image of the differential **out of** `c`. The two corrections in\n`finrank_bump_add` are both of this form, at adjacent cells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.range_transport_le_ker","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.range_transport_le_ker","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/EulerCharacteristic.lean#L132-L143","doc":"**`d ∘ d = 0`, transported.** `PagedSS.d_comp_d` is stated at\n`next (prev c)`, which is `c` only propositionally, so the fact that the\nincoming image lies in `ker d_c` needs the transport spelt out. Stating it\nwith the equation `h` as a hypothesis lets `subst` do the work. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.reindex_rfl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.reindex_rfl","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/EulerCharacteristic.lean#L129-L130","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.sgn_bump","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.sgn_bump","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/EulerCharacteristic.lean#L121-L122","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.sgn_next","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.sgn_next","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/EulerCharacteristic.lean#L117-L119","doc":"The sign flips along the differential — the source of the cancellation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.sgn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.sgn","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/EulerCharacteristic.lean#L114-L115","doc":"`(−1)^{p+q}`, the total-degree sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.instDecidableEqCellIndex_folio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.instDecidableEqCellIndex_folio","kind":"instance","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/EulerCharacteristic.lean#L108-L112","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.prev_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.prev_injective","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/EulerCharacteristic.lean#L105-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.prev_next","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.prev_next","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/EulerCharacteristic.lean#L96-L103","doc":"`prev` inverts `next` on the other side. `PagedSpectralSequence` has\n`next_prev`; this is what makes `prev` **injective**, which is what the sum\nreindexing needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.deg_bump","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.deg_bump","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/EulerCharacteristic.lean#L92-L94","doc":"Page-turning keeps the bidegree, hence the total degree and its sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.deg_prev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.deg_prev","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/EulerCharacteristic.lean#L87-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.deg_next","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.deg_next","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/EulerCharacteristic.lean#L79-L85","doc":"**The differential raises total degree by one.** This is what makes each\npage a cochain complex in the total grading, and it is the reason the two\ncorrection terms below carry opposite signs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.CellIndex.deg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.EulerCharacteristic.CellIndex.deg","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/EulerCharacteristic.lean#L75-L77","doc":"Total degree `p + q`. `CellIndex`'s own docstring names `q` the\n\"total-complement degree\" for exactly this sum. ","signatureChunk":0}]}